        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Hormuz tensions highlight pressure tactics in US-Iran negotiations Middle East Issued on: 18/04/2026 - 16:22 H. A. Hellyer, senior fellow in geopolitics at the Royal United Services Institute, was France 24’s guest and analysed the renewed tensions between the United States and Iran in the Strait of Hormuz as a strategy of mutual pressure amid ongoing negotiations. While talks are set to continue in Islamabad, both sides are using leverage, particularly the US blockade of Iranian port, to strengthen their positions, making any quick breakthrough unlikely. Turkey’s economy hit as Syrians return home 18/04/2026 Middle East French soldier killed in attack on UN mission in southern Lebanon, officials say 18/04/2026 Middle East Strait of Hormuz : Iran to block transit until US lifts its blockade 18/04/2026 Middle East Middle East : Fragile US-Iran talks hinge on nuclear and Hormuz disputes 18/04/2026 Middle East The Gaza Strip grapples with a major garbage, health crisis 18/04/2026 Middle East Middle East : What to expect from the truce between Lebanon and Israel ? 18/04/2026 Middle East Iran closes Hormuz Strait again over US blockade with ships mid-transit 18/04/2026 Middle East Iran declares the Strait of Hormuz 'completely open' amid fragile ceasefire 18/04/2026 Middle East Southern Lebanon residents return home to devastation after ceasefire 18/04/2026 Middle East"
