        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Turkey’s economy hit as Syrians return home Middle East Issued on: 18/04/2026 - 16:18 Since the end of the war in Syria last year, many Syrians have left Turkey to return home. Of the 3.6 million refugees living in the country, more than half a million are believed to have already gone back. These departures are weakening the Turkish economy, which relies heavily on low-cost labour, particularly in the textile and agricultural sectors. In the south-east, in Gaziantep, half of the garment workshops closed last year due to a shortage of workers. A report by Jenna Le Bras and Adrià Rocha Cutiller. French soldier killed in attack on UN mission in southern Lebanon, officials say 18/04/2026 Middle East Strait of Hormuz : Iran to block transit until US lifts its blockade 18/04/2026 Middle East Middle East : Fragile US-Iran talks hinge on nuclear and Hormuz disputes 18/04/2026 Middle East The Gaza Strip grapples with a major garbage, health crisis 18/04/2026 Middle East Middle East : What to expect from the truce between Lebanon and Israel ? 18/04/2026 Middle East Iran closes Hormuz Strait again over US blockade with ships mid-transit 18/04/2026 Middle East Iran declares the Strait of Hormuz 'completely open' amid fragile ceasefire 18/04/2026 Middle East Southern Lebanon residents return home to devastation after ceasefire 18/04/2026 Middle East \"We are just displaced and we have to go back\" : Lebanese return to southern villages 18/04/2026 Middle East"
